"kind":"text","text":". We can build the shortest solution by permuting the strings and then trying to 'attach' them to each other. I.e., we need to find the longest overlapping segments at the end of string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the beginning of string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The obvious brute force solution won't run in time. However, we can use a hash function to help us calculate the result in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time, where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"min"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"len"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")). The hash function that I used was the polynomial "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hash"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subsc